Description: GHSA-m8rr-4c36-8gq4 (CVE-2026-7258): every char handed to a ctype.h function (isalpha(), isdigit(), isspace(), tolower(), toupper() and the others) is cast to unsigned char: a byte of 0x80 and above made a negative argument, which the C standard leaves undefined and some C libraries use as an index before their table (FreeBSD and glibc check or allow it). The places of 7.4 that 5.6 does not have are left out.
Origin: port of php-src commits b44c4c80d8a7 (03.05.2026, Ilija Tovilo) and 2c4b0c49d017 (25.10.2026: the -d value check of the CLI, CGI, FPM and phpdbg SAPIs) of the PHP 7.4 security branch of Remi Collet (remicollet/php-src-security PHP-7.4-security-backports); in 5.6 also in ext/gd/libgd/xbm.c (gd_xbm.c in 7.4) and in the files that re2c made from the changed .re files

